WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.157
<v Examiner>Three marks.

2
00:00:02.157 --> 00:00:05.704
<v Examiner>Describe paracetamol: its drug class, what it's used for,

3
00:00:05.704 --> 00:00:08.194
<v Examiner>and one important nursing consideration.

4
00:00:08.644 --> 00:00:12.230
Class: paracetamol is an analgesic and an antipyretic.

5
00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:16.879
It's a general sale medicine, so people can buy it at the supermarket.

6
00:00:17.329 --> 00:00:19.964
Use: mild to moderate pain, and fever.

7
00:00:19.964 --> 00:00:21.074
Not severe pain.

8
00:00:21.074 --> 00:00:25.860
Joan's example for maximal efficacy: paracetamol reaches its ceiling,

9
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.496
and more of it won't give more relief.

10
00:00:28.496 --> 00:00:31.409
After that you move to another drug class.

11
00:00:31.859 --> 00:00:35.136
The nursing considerations, any one for the mark.

12
00:00:35.136 --> 00:00:39.350
The dose: for an adult, up to one gram every four to six hours,

13
00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:42.360
no more than four grams in twenty-four hours.

14
00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:45.838
For a child, fifteen milligrams per kilogram a dose.

15
00:00:45.838 --> 00:00:50.587
In overdose it damages the liver, and the antidote is N-acetylcysteine,

16
00:00:50.587 --> 00:00:51.858
often called N A C.

17
00:00:51.858 --> 00:00:55.537
And the one Joan teaches: check for hidden paracetamol.

18
00:00:55.537 --> 00:00:58.079
Panadol and Panadeine both contain it,

19
00:00:58.079 --> 00:01:02.627
so a patient who thinks they're two different drugs can double-dose.

20
00:01:02.627 --> 00:01:05.169
That's why you teach the generic name.

21
00:01:05.619 --> 00:01:09.364
Paracetamol: analgesic and antipyretic, general sale.

22
00:01:09.364 --> 00:01:11.625
Mild to moderate pain and fever.

23
00:01:11.625 --> 00:01:16.147
Adults up to one gram four- to six-hourly, max four grams a day;

24
00:01:16.147 --> 00:01:19.044
children fifteen milligrams per kilogram.

25
00:01:19.044 --> 00:01:22.436
Overdose harms the liver; the antidote is N A C.

26
00:01:22.436 --> 00:01:25.757
Watch for hidden paracetamol in other products.
